Falsifies `page_frames::verification::the_used_count_is_the_number_of_set_bits`.

The defect: `alloc_contiguous` counts one frame used for a run of `count`. It reads as a
bookkeeping slip, and every allocator harness but this one builds the struct with a counter it
never reads.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(fa.used, set_bits)`, on a run of two or more frames.
`Stats::free` then reports frames that are not free, which the kernel prints and a test boots on.

diff --git a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/page_frames/src/lib.rs
@@ -298,3 +298,3 @@
                 }
-                self.used += count;
+                self.used += 1;
                 return Some(PageFrame(self.base + run_start as u64 * FRAME_SIZE));
